implementationPlan.description:
Adversarial self-review of this row's diff, once (load adversarial-self-review). Record it in complete_step.
(a) Fail closed: no record state other than ABSENT or LEGACY can let a non-verified-local declaration answer 'legacy'. A failing confirmer never downgrades.
(b) Restart semantics: an allowed downgrade never changes the current session's answer.
(c) Store safety:
  - names never come from input;
  - a link, wrong mode, foreign uid or oversize file is refused;
  - the temp-plus-rename write is atomic and leaves no temp file on failure;
  - a root inside the project writes nothing.
(d) Concurrency: two VS Code windows on one project. Each writes the whole record by atomic rename, so the last writer wins with a valid record, and neither can produce a torn file.
(e) The strict-map suites pass: no new top-level import (grep the import block).
(f) Mutation check in a scratch copy of the Linux snapshot:
  - let UNTRUSTED read as LEGACY: P6 must fail;
  - persist on 'Keep Protected': P3 must fail;
  - drop the inside-project guard: P7 must fail;
  - skip the session pin after allow: P5 must fail.
  Then confirm the restored copy passes.
(g) Name in the handoff what task-648a5916 reuses: useProtectedStateRoot, projectStateKey, protectedStateName(kind, key), readProtectedState and writeProtectedState.
